  "articleSummary": "The article provides an analytical comparison of NVMe SSD cloud options, focusing on AWS EC2 i3 instances (e.g., i3.large and i3.2xlarge) as the most cost-effective and highest-performing choices for ultra-fast storage. It presents benchmark data showing that while NVMe SSDs deliver over 1 GB/s speeds, real-world network performance often falls short of advertised rates (e.g., \"up to 10 Gb/s\" achieving only ~60–80 MB/s). The tone is data-driven and evaluative, aimed at cloud architects and developers seeking price-vs.-I/O performance guidance. Key findings include specific pricing (e.g., $110/month for a 475 GB NVMe SSD) and head-to-head charts comparing throughput across providers.",
